-- title:
--   Deligne–Serre lifting lemma for weight-two Hecke algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and suppose $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ has an integral structure in the sense of [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6): the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule generated by those cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers is the whole space. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ N}`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to the primes $\ell \nmid N$ (the $U_q$-generators are excluded, the excluded set being exactly the primes dividing $N$). Let $\mathfrak{m}_1 \subset \mathbb{T}$ be a maximal ideal and $p$ a natural number whose image in $\mathbb{T}$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_1$ ($p$ is not assumed prime). The conclusion asserts the existence of $f \in S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ satisfying `IsNormalizedEigenform` (first $q$-coefficient $1$, multiplicativity of $q$-coefficients at coprime indices, and the two prime-power recursions according as the prime divides $N$ or not) and of a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}'$ of the ring $\overline{\mathbb{Z}} =$ `integralClosure ℤ ℂ` of algebraic integers, with $p \in \mathfrak{m}'$, such that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ and every $b \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $T_\ell - b \in \mathfrak{m}_1$ there is $a \in \overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ with $a = a_\ell(f)$, the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $f$, and $a - b \in \mathfrak{m}'$.
--
--   This is the Deligne–Serre lifting lemma in the form used for weight two: a maximal ideal of the integral Hecke algebra with residue characteristic dividing $p$ is realised by the Hecke eigenvalue system of a characteristic-zero normalised eigenform, congruent to it modulo a maximal ideal of $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ above $p$. It feeds the passage from an abstract mod $p$ Hecke eigensystem to a weight-two eigenform, being cited by [`FLT.AbstractIntegralStructure.exists_weight_two_eigenform_congruent_of_heckeT_congr`](thm.html#FLT.AbstractIntegralStructure.exists_weight_two_eigenform_congruent_of_heckeT_congr).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_isNormalizedEigenform_congruent_of_isMaximal.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_IntegralStructure

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.exists_isNormalizedEigenform_congruent_of_isMaximal {N : ℕ} [NeZero N] (hN : CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2) (𝔪₁ : Ideal (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ N})) (h𝔪₁ : 𝔪₁.IsMaximal) {p : ℕ} (hp𝔪 : (p : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ N}) ∈ 𝔪₁) : ∃ (f : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2) (_ : f.IsNormalizedEigenform) (𝔪' : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ ℂ)), 𝔪'.IsMaximal ∧ (p : integralClosure ℤ ℂ) ∈ 𝔪' ∧ ∀ (ℓ : ℕ) (hℓ : ℓ.Prime) (hℓN : ¬ ℓ ∣ N) (b : ℤ), CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T hℓ hℓN hℓN - (b : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ N}) ∈ 𝔪₁ → ∃ a : integralClosure ℤ ℂ, (a : ℂ) = ModularFormClass.qCoeff f ℓ ∧ a - (b : integralClosure ℤ ℂ) ∈ 𝔪' := by sorry
